## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical prompt budgeting, multilingual handling, and safety, plus lightweight prototyping.

## Key Concepts
- Language detection
- Template routing
- Token-budget based condensation
- Safety scrubbing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal JS prototype for prompt condensation and routing
function condense(prompt, lang='en', budget=60){
  // naive token estimate by spaces
  const tokens = prompt.trim().split(/\\s+/);
  const trimmed = tokens.length > budget ? tokens.slice(0,budget).join(' ') + '...' : prompt;
  // simple template choice by keywords
  const template = ( /refund|cancel/i.test(prompt) ? 'concise' : 'empathetic');
  return {template, prompt: trimmed};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you unit test the condensation and template routing?
- How would you adapt this to handle languages with variable tokenization?

## Why This Is Asked

Gauges practical, client-side prompt evaluation with safety and tone controls for high-stakes brands. Focuses on a beginner-friendly rubric and a concrete routing prototype, suitable for scalable chat systems.

## Key Concepts

- Prompt scoring rubrics
- Client-side routing logic
- Safety and bias considerations
- Minimal unit testing for NLP-ish logic

## Code Example

```javascript
function routePrompt(input){
  const lower = input.toLowerCase();
  const clarity = /order|status|refund/.test(lower) ? 4 : 2;
  const safety = !lower.includes('password') ? 4 : 2;
  const bias = /(racial|gender|biased)/.test(lower) ? 5 : 1;
  if (clarity >= 4 && safety >= 4 && bias <= 2) return 'concise';
  if (lower.includes('please') || lower.includes('sorry')) return 'empathetic';
  return 'authoritative';
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you extend scoring to multilingual prompts?
- How would you evaluate and mitigate bias in edge prompts?
- How would you test the classifier with real user prompts?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to extend routing with governance constraints and to design testable prototypes.

## Key Concepts
- multi-module routing with governance
- signal design: intent, data_sensitivity, governance_policy
- edge-case handling: conflicts, missing role

## Code Example
```javascript
function route(prompt, signals){
  if (signals.governance_policy === 'restrict') return {module:'Data-Governance', payload:{prompt}};
  if (signals.data_sensitivity === 'PII') return {module:'PII-redactor', payload:{prompt}};
  return {module:'SQL-builder', payload:{prompt}};
}
module.exports = route;
```

